	Actually, it's pretty easy to imagine a more effective pet.
Almost anything even moderately tough makes a better pet than an
arch-lich. Pets won't use a lot of special attacks, so lich pets have
basically nothing but their freezing touch, which is decent but not
amazingly good. A pet arch-lich can't kill a blue jelly (which won't
stop it from trying).

	On top of that, arch-liches teleport, which makes it difficult
to keep them out of places you don't want them in. Like, to stop them
from killing the priest you're trying to donate to. Or your Quest
Leader.

	And, as non-eaters, they're difficult to keep tame, and if they
go feral, they suddenly remember how to use all those special powers,
which makes them a much bigger threat to you than they ever will be to
your enemies.

	I'd recommend taking him down to the bottom of the Mines and
ditching him. Or blessed-genocide L and don't worry about the collateral
damage. And whatever you do, don't take him into Home 1.

